  "title": "Why do companies love posting viral videos of their workers planting ...",
  "description": "Why do companies love posting viral videos of their workers planting thousands of trees where a intact biodiverse forest used to be. The answer is simple. Greed. Almost all of the old growth redwood forest has been logged already , only 4% remains. The story is similar for every old growth tree in North America. Protecting mature and old growth forests should be a number priority globally these trees are massive carbon batteries that protect us from the effects of climate change. And are crucial for wildlife biodiversity.  California and Canada are covered in unhealthy second growth monoculture lumber forests that are logged every 50 years. These forests make wildfires worse and have 80% less wildlife then old growth. Stop letting companies trick you into letting them destroy the little old growth left , so they can plant another forest factory farm. Protect old growth forests.  #oldgrowth #redwoods #forest #ecology #california #oldgrowthforest #logging #redwood #trees #bigtree #capitalism #redwoodforest #botany #fire #eco #nature #treeroots #native #tree #nativeplants #nativeplanttok #nativehabitatproject #plantlover #cali #rainforestfacts ",
